# 3. Introduction

This project demonstrates the implementation of an automated Continuous Integration and Continuous Deployment (CI/CD) pipeline for a Flask-based Student Management System.

The application uses Flask as the backend framework and MongoDB Atlas as the database. Docker is used to containerize the application. GitHub Actions automates the testing, Docker image creation, image push to Amazon Elastic Container Registry (ECR), deployment to an Amazon EC2 instance, application health verification, and email notifications.

The complete CI/CD workflow eliminates the need to manually build, test and deploy the application after every code change.

The implemented flow is:

**Developer → GitHub → GitHub Actions → Automated Tests → Docker Build → AWS ECR → AWS EC2 → Health Check → Email Notification**

---

# 4. Project Objectives

The main objectives of this assignment are:

1. Develop and maintain a Flask web application.
2. Connect the Flask application with MongoDB.
3. Write automated test cases using Pytest.
4. Containerize the Flask application using Docker.
5. Create a GitHub Actions CI/CD workflow.
6. Automatically execute application tests.
7. Build a Docker image automatically.
8. Push the Docker image to AWS ECR.
9. Deploy the application on AWS EC2.
10. Verify the deployed application using a health-check endpoint.
11. Implement success email notification.
12. Implement failure email notification.
13. Document the complete implementation with screenshots.

