# 12. Docker Containerization

The Flask application is containerized using Docker.

The Dockerfile defines:

* Base Python image
* Application dependencies
* Application source code
* Application port
* Application startup command

The application runs inside the Docker container on:

```text
Port 5000
```

The Docker container allows the application to run consistently across different environments.

---

# 13. Docker Image

The Docker image is built as part of the CI/CD pipeline.

The image is tagged using the Git commit SHA.

This provides version tracking.

For example:

```text
flask-practice:<commit-sha>
```

Using the commit SHA provides traceability between:

```text
Git Commit
      ↓
Docker Image
      ↓
ECR
      ↓
EC2 Deployment
```

Therefore, it is possible to identify exactly which source-code commit was deployed.

