# 17. GitHub Actions CI/CD Workflow

The CI/CD workflow is stored inside:

```text
.github/workflows/ci-cd.yml
```

The workflow automates the complete deployment process.

The main stages are:

```text
Checkout Source Code
        ↓
Install Dependencies
        ↓
Run Tests
        ↓
Build Docker Image
        ↓
Login to AWS ECR
        ↓
Push Image to ECR
        ↓
Connect to EC2
        ↓
Pull Latest Image
        ↓
Stop/Remove Existing Container
        ↓
Start New Container
        ↓
Health Check
        ↓
Send Email Notification
```

---

# 18. CI/CD Pipeline Stages

## Stage 1 – Checkout

GitHub Actions checks out the latest source code from the repository.

---

## Stage 2 – Test

Dependencies are installed and automated tests are executed.

If tests fail, the pipeline stops.

No deployment is performed when the test stage fails.

---

## Stage 3 – Docker Build

After successful testing, the Docker image is built.

The image is tagged using the commit SHA.

---

## Stage 4 – ECR Login

GitHub Actions authenticates with AWS ECR.

The AWS credentials are stored securely in GitHub Secrets.

---

## Stage 5 – Push Image

The Docker image is pushed to:

```text
flask-practice
```

in AWS ECR.

---

## Stage 6 – EC2 Deployment

The workflow connects to the EC2 server using SSH.

The existing Flask container is replaced with the newly built image.

---

## Stage 7 – Health Check

After deployment, the workflow checks:

```text
http://localhost:5000/health
```

The expected HTTP status is:

```text
200
```

The expected response is:

```json
{
  "status": "healthy"
}
```

---

## Stage 8 – Email Notification

After the workflow finishes:

* Success email is sent when deployment succeeds.
* Failure email is sent when a pipeline stage fails.

---

# 19. GitHub Secrets

Sensitive information is stored in GitHub Secrets.

The project uses secrets such as:

```text
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY
ECR_REGISTRY
EC2_HOST
EC2_USER
EC2_SSH_KEY
MONGO_URI
SECRET_KEY
```

The values are never hard-coded into the repository.

