# 28. Security Considerations

The following security practices were followed:

### 28.1 Secrets

Credentials are stored using GitHub Secrets.

### 28.2 MongoDB Credentials

The MongoDB URI is provided through environment variables.

### 28.3 AWS Credentials

AWS access credentials are not committed to GitHub.

### 28.4 SSH Key

The EC2 SSH private key is stored securely as a GitHub Secret.

### 28.5 Environment Variables

Sensitive configuration is managed through environment variables.

### 28.6 Screenshot Security

Screenshots submitted with the assignment should not expose:

* AWS secret access keys
* MongoDB passwords
* GitHub secret values
* SSH private keys
* SMTP passwords
* Application secrets

---

# 29. Error Handling and Troubleshooting

During implementation, several common deployment issues were identified and resolved.

## MongoDB Authentication Error

An incorrect MongoDB configuration resulted in:

```text
Authentication failed
```

The MongoDB connection configuration was corrected and the health endpoint subsequently returned:

```text
HTTP 200
```

---

## Docker Container Conflict

If a container named `flask-app` already exists, Docker may report a container-name conflict.

The old container can be removed before starting a new one.

---

## EC2 Docker Verification

The running container was verified using:

```bash
docker ps
```

---

## Health Check

The application was verified using:

```bash
curl -i http://localhost:5000/health
```

Final successful result:

```text
HTTP/1.1 200 OK
```

```json
{
  "status": "healthy"
}
```

---

# 30. Final CI/CD Architecture

The implemented architecture is:

```text
                  Developer
                      |
                      v
                GitHub Repository
                      |
                      v
              GitHub Actions
                      |
              +-------+-------+
              |               |
              v               v
           Pytest         Docker Build
              |               |
              +-------+-------+
                      |
                      v
                 AWS ECR
                      |
                      v
                 AWS EC2
                      |
                      v
               Docker Container
                 flask-app
                      |
                      v
             Flask Application
                      |
                      v
                MongoDB Atlas
                      |
                      v
                Health Check
                      |
             +--------+--------+
             |                 |
          Success            Failure
             |                 |
             v                 v
        Success Email     Failure Email
```

---

# 31. End-to-End Workflow

The final automated process is:

```text
1. Developer pushes code to GitHub
              ↓
2. GitHub Actions starts
              ↓
3. Python environment is prepared
              ↓
4. Dependencies are installed
              ↓
5. Pytest tests are executed
              ↓
6. Docker image is built
              ↓
7. AWS ECR authentication occurs
              ↓
8. Image is pushed to ECR
              ↓
9. GitHub Actions connects to EC2
              ↓
10. New image is pulled
              ↓
11. Existing container is replaced
              ↓
12. New Flask container starts
              ↓
13. /health endpoint is tested
              ↓
14. HTTP 200 confirms deployment
              ↓
15. Success email is sent
```

If any required stage fails:

```text
Pipeline Failure
       ↓
Failure Notification
       ↓
Deployment is reported as unsuccessful
```

