# 35. Final Conclusion

The Flask Student Management System was successfully containerized using Docker and deployed on AWS EC2 through an automated GitHub Actions CI/CD pipeline.

The implementation includes automated testing, Docker image creation, Amazon ECR image storage, EC2 deployment, MongoDB Atlas integration, application health verification and email notifications.

The final pipeline successfully demonstrates:

```text
Code Commit
    ↓
Automated Test
    ↓
Docker Build
    ↓
ECR Push
    ↓
EC2 Deployment
    ↓
Health Check
    ↓
Email Notification
```

The successful health check returned HTTP 200 with a healthy status, confirming that the deployed Flask application was operational.

Both successful and failure scenarios were also tested, demonstrating that the pipeline can provide appropriate notifications for deployment success and failure.

Therefore, the project successfully demonstrates an end-to-end DevOps CI/CD implementation using:

**Flask + Python + MongoDB Atlas + Pytest + Docker + GitHub Actions + AWS ECR + AWS EC2 + IAM + Email Notifications.**

